      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Verify Ollama API keys on an authenticated endpoint",
        "body": "## Summary\n- stop treating the public `/api/tags` catalog as API-key verification\n- validate the key against authenticated `/api/web_search` without performing a search\n- fetch the public model catalog only after authentication succeeds\n\n## Live proof\nRedacted live Ollama requests on 2026-07-06:\n\n```text\nGET /api/tags, no Authorization             -> 200, 34 models\nGET /api/tags, Bearer codexbar-proof-invalid -> 200, 34 models\nPOST /api/web_search, invalid Bearer, empty query -> 401 {\"error\":\"Unauthorized\"}\n```\n\nThis proves `/api/tags` accepts an invalid key and cannot verify credentials, while `/api/web_search` rejects the same key before query validation. No real key, account data, browser cookie, or Keychain access was used.\n\nOfficial authentication reference: https://docs.ollama.com/api/authentication\n\n## Tests\n- `swift test --disable-sandbox --filter OllamaUsageFetcherRetryMappingTests` (8 passed)\n- changed Swift files pass SwiftFormat and SwiftLint strict\n- `git diff --check upstream/main...HEAD`\n\n## Commits\n- exactly 3: implementation, tests, documentation",
